1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,710
When a Set turns Yes, does anything different tend to happen next,

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:05,612
compared with ordinary days?

3
00:00:06,046 --> 00:00:10,442
Each time a Set first turns Yes, we look at the next ten daily candles.

4
00:00:10,492 --> 00:00:12,424
We compare them with ordinary days:

5
00:00:12,444 --> 00:00:16,872
the same asset, the same year, and the same side of its long-term average.

6
00:00:16,922 --> 00:00:24,433
Twenty-five coins and sixty-one large US equities, from 2014 to October 2024.

7
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:27,473
Every provided Set carries the result.

8
00:00:27,523 --> 00:00:30,297
Open more, and the last line is What followed.

9
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:32,441
Tap it for the numbers.

10
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:36,162
Breakout with volume turned Yes almost nineteen hundred times.

11
00:00:36,212 --> 00:00:40,357
Price rose a typical move before falling one fifty-one percent of the time,

12
00:00:40,377 --> 00:00:42,954
against fifty percent on comparable days.

13
00:00:43,405 --> 00:00:46,329
Under it, coins and equities, each on its own:

14
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:49,602
here, no clear difference in either, and none between them.

15
00:00:50,037 --> 00:00:52,684
Every study ends in one of four verdicts:

16
00:00:52,734 --> 00:00:54,335
too few to judge,

17
00:00:54,385 --> 00:00:56,029
no clear difference,

18
00:00:56,079 --> 00:00:58,214
some difference, not established,

19
00:00:58,264 --> 00:01:00,249
or a consistent difference.

20
00:01:00,689 --> 00:01:03,400
Most simple setups show no clear difference.

21
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:08,251
That's an honest, useful answer: they describe a situation; they don't predict one.

22
00:01:08,684 --> 00:01:11,181
Trend alignment is the interesting one.

23
00:01:11,231 --> 00:01:13,680
After the daily and weekly trends first agree,

24
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:16,630
price did a little worse than on comparable days.

25
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:20,479
Often the weekly trend confirms a move after much of it has happened.

26
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:24,356
Make your own copy and save it: its study comes with it.

27
00:01:24,406 --> 00:01:28,567
In Signal Sets, the card also shows the three periods side by side,

28
00:01:41,703 --> 00:01:44,350
and every asset on its own, with a luck check.

29
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:49,137
Ten assets look unusual for this Set, where luck alone typically makes about four.

30
00:01:49,187 --> 00:01:51,450
A place to look closer, not proof.

31
00:01:51,885 --> 00:01:54,126
Your own Sets can be studied too:

32
00:01:54,176 --> 00:01:57,506
open one in Signal Sets, and tap Study this Set.

33
00:01:57,556 --> 00:02:00,821
When it's ready, a note arrives in your notifications.
